            <ArticleTitle>'2' much mitral tissue.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>189</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/ejechocard/jep176</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 73-year-old female patient was referred for evaluation after suffering an atypical chest pain. Physical examination and ECG were normal. The echocardiogram showed a normal ventricular function. Attached to the anterior leaflet an accessory mitral valve tissue was identified. In systole, this mitral tissue creates an image that looks like the 'number 2'.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
